from types import ProofRouteConsequenceAssessment

a1_skill_1: Skill[ProofRouteConsequenceAssessment] = skill_artifact[ProofRouteConsequenceAssessment](
    "proof-bridge-object-forger",
    "0.0.0+repository-conversion",
    "proof-bridge-object-forger",
    "Design missing mathematical carriers, bridge objects, representations, invariants, interfaces, or transfer laws for blocked proof routes. Use when another lemma is not enough and a new object must mediate the route.",
    "---\nname: proof-bridge-object-forger\ndescription: Design missing mathematical carriers, bridge objects, representations, invariants, interfaces, or transfer laws for blocked proof routes. Use when another lemma is not enough and a new object must mediate the route.\n---\n\n# Proof Bridge Object Forger\n\nForge inspectable bridge objects rather than broad analogies.\n\n## Critical Conceptual Depth\n\nA bridge object is valuable only if it mediates a real conceptual gap. It\nshould expose the interface where two structures almost meet but do not yet\nmatch: geometry to positivity, finite regulator to continuum claim, witness\nfamily to lower-bound carrier, proof system to semantic complexity class, or\nlocal calculation to global invariant.\n\n## Value Signal\n\nState the bridge's conceptual payoff: what it makes representable, what it\nexplains, what it unifies, and what new theorem or obstruction it could carry.\nAlso state what would make the bridge worthless, especially if it simply\ndefines the target property into existence.\n\n## Mathematical Invariants\n\n- Name the source object, target object, proposed bridge object, preserved\n  invariants, broken invariants, and boundary regimes.\n- State construction requirements and first counterexample or failure regime.\n- Forbid bridges whose definition already includes the desired target\n  conclusion; route those to transfer-substance audit.\n\n## Epistemic Discipline\n\n- Cite source artifacts, KB ids, existing objects that fail, and explicit\n  unknowns.\n- Mark the bridge as conjectural, proof-obligation, blocked, promoted,\n  demoted, or quarantined.\n- Treat analogies as search hints until they produce an object, invariant, and\n  validation handoff.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn:\n\n- `bridge_object_name`\n- `source_object`\n- `target_object`\n- `why_existing_objects_fail`\n- `construction_requirements`\n- `preserved_invariants`\n- `broken_invariants`\n- `edge_case_or_counterexample`\n- `validation_obligations`\n- `first_falsifier`\n- `evidence`\n- `validation_handoff`\n\n## Failure/Demotion\n\nDemote named objects with no construction requirements, no invariant map, no\nedge case, or no target-scoped validation handoff. Quarantine bridges that\nsolve a different problem or change the target domain while preserving\nnotation.\n\n## Packaged PRISM Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly the generated `ProofObligationEntrypointHypothesis` JSON object. Do not paraphrase closed variant values.\n\n- Follow the exact generated JSON schema without extra fields.\n",
    "{\"agents/openai.yaml\":\"\"}",
)
